  "body": "@tyoshino is really good at plugging coverage gaps in our test suite :D. But, it'd be good to get a computer to find them for us.\n\nNormally I would use [istanbul](http://npmjs.org/istanbul) but our usage of ES6 via Traceur throws a wrench into things. We could probably get Istanbul running on the transpiled output, which would be better than nothing. But it will not be as easy to use and digest as coverage reports of the source. There would be lots of \"uncovered\" areas that are just part of the Traceur output and logic.\n\nThere may be some way to use source maps to map the coverage back? Or maybe someone has put together some sort of ES6 code coverage tool? This needs investigation. Will ask around on Twitter and the Traceur Google Group.\n\n/cc @arv @johnjbarton\n",
